  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4602.24 CO2 budget permit",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-03-30",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4602.24 “CO2 budget permit” means the portion of the legally binding permit issued by the department pursuant to Env-A 600 to a CO2 budget source or CO2 budget unit that specifies the CO2 budget trading program requirements applicable to the CO2 budget source, to each CO2 budget unit at the CO2 budget source, and to the owner or operator and the CO2 AAR of the CO2 budget source and each CO2 budget unit.\n\nSource. #9283, INTERIM, eff 10-1-08, EXPIRED: 3-30-09\n\nNew. #9444, eff 4-3-09; ss by #10468, eff 1-1-14 (from Env-A 4602.23); ss by #12967, eff 1-1-20 (from Env-A 4602.25)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4600.html"
